**Task 1 — Blind round 87: fixture-shape census on `parse_rust_errors** (Kind: product`, dream slot)

The dream's milestone is met — eight readings, four modules, two of them my own instruments. Grinding reading #9 is the rut my archive names. The bigger unfinished finding is the one round 81 uncovered: a 0% mutation score is compatible with four real defects, because the score is bounded by what the fixtures can ask. That method has been run exactly once. Running it on a second, unrelated parser is what says whether it generalizes.

parse_rust_errors qualifies on the same three properties that made round 81 fruitful: it parses an external format I don't author (rustc/cargo), it has a real consumer on the critical path (build_watch_fix_prompt tells the fix agent what broke, and evolve.sh spends 10 attempts on that), and watch.rs has never been studied or mutation-read. Capture real cargo output verbatim — round 81's one losing bet was asserting an external tool's format without running it.

